From ce5a1c519b93f50d7ba4cad1323fb9a25a8a4549 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:50:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Thylacine CL-4b: getMainExecutable returns an absolute
 argv0 directly

getprogpath routes through test_dir -> realpath(), which fails on Thylacine
(musl realpath needs /proc/self/fd, absent here). That dropped clang's
InstalledDir to empty, so the driver built an empty-path -cc1 command and
posix_spawn failed EINVAL -- clang could print --version but never compile.
An absolute argv0 IS the executable path; return it directly (like the
executable is actually named), realpath-free.
---
 llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc b/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
index 9a6b3849f..89cc308fa 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
+++ b/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
@@ -330,7 +330,17 @@ std::string getMainExecutable(const char *argv0, void *MainAddr) {
   // Thylacine has no /proc/self/exe, and dladdr is inert in a static musl
   // binary (dlopen/dladdr are ENOSYS stubs). Resolve from argv[0] + $PATH --
   // the classical detection, like OpenBSD/Haiku. clang's InstalledDir +
-  // resource-dir discovery depend on this returning a real path.
+  // resource-dir discovery + cc1/ld.lld sub-spawn all depend on this returning
+  // a real path.
+  //
+  // An ABSOLUTE argv0 IS the executable path -- return it directly. getprogpath
+  // routes through test_dir -> realpath(), which fails on Thylacine (musl
+  // realpath needs /proc/self/fd, absent here), so the general path drops
+  // InstalledDir to "" -> clang builds an empty-path -cc1 command -> posix_spawn
+  // fails EINVAL. The direct return is also how the executable is actually named
+  // (joey spawns absolute paths); a $PATH search would only re-derive it.
+  if (argv0 && argv0[0] == '/')
+    return argv0;
   char exe_path[PATH_MAX];
   if (getprogpath(exe_path, argv0) != NULL)
     return exe_path;
